  ($qb$HEAIL-PWD-SJT-048$qb$, $qb$A7-02$qb$, $qb$SJT$qb$, $qb$You notice that a form your team uses asks for a customer's phone number twice, in two different places. Staff sometimes enter different numbers. How do you handle it?$qb$, $qb$Raise it with whoever owns the form, and check what each field feeds into first$qb$, $qb$Raise it with whoever owns the form, showing where the two entries conflict$qb$, $qb$Tell the team to make sure both fields always match when completing it$qb$, $qb$Ask the team to use the first field only and leave the second blank$qb$, $qb$Leave it, since staff can usually tell which number is the right one$qb$, 5, 3, 2, 1, 0, true),
