  ($qb$HEAIL-PSP-MCQ-018$qb$, $qb$A7-03$qb$, $qb$MCQ$qb$, $qb$You are organising a training day in six weeks. What should you settle first?$qb$, $qb$The things that take longest to arrange, such as the venue and the trainer$qb$, $qb$The date and the venue, since everything else depends on those two$qb$, $qb$The content, since that determines what kind of venue you need$qb$, $qb$The list of who is attending, so you know what size room to book$qb$, $qb$The budget, since that limits every other choice you will make$qb$, 5, 3, 2, 1, 0, true),
  ($qb$HEAIL-PSP-MCQ-019$qb$, $qb$A7-03$qb$, $qb$MCQ$qb$, $qb$Your team is taking on a new task that only one person currently knows how to do. What should your plan cover?$qb$, $qb$Training a second person now, before the first one is unavailable$qb$, $qb$Writing the task down in enough detail for someone else to follow$qb$, $qb$Identifying who would be the best second person to learn it$qb$, $qb$Asking the person to be available if they are ever needed while away$qb$, $qb$Dealing with it if and when that person is actually absent$qb$, 5, 3, 2, 1, 0, true),
  ($qb$HEAIL-PSP-MCQ-020$qb$, $qb$A7-03$qb$, $qb$MCQ$qb$, $qb$A project has ten tasks. Three of them cannot start until a supplier delivers. What should you do?$qb$, $qb$Confirm the delivery date now and sequence those three around it$qb$, $qb$Start the seven tasks that do not depend on the delivery$qb$, $qb$Ask the supplier to confirm the delivery is still on schedule$qb$, $qb$Plan all ten tasks assuming the delivery arrives when promised$qb$, $qb$Wait for the delivery before committing to a detailed plan$qb$, 5, 3, 2, 1, 0, true),
