  ($qb$HEAIL-ECF-MCQ-018$qb$, $qb$A7-01$qb$, $qb$MCQ$qb$, $qb$You have finished a report and sent it to your manager. What still needs to happen?$qb$, $qb$Ask them to confirm receipt and whether anything further is needed from you$qb$, $qb$Send a short note asking them to confirm that they have received it$qb$, $qb$Ask them to let you know if there is anything else they need$qb$, $qb$Wait to hear back, since they will contact you if there is a problem$qb$, $qb$Nothing, since the work is finished and has been sent on$qb$, 5, 3, 2, 1, 0, true),
  ($qb$HEAIL-ECF-MCQ-019$qb$, $qb$A7-01$qb$, $qb$MCQ$qb$, $qb$You have five tasks in progress and none of them finished. What is the best response?$qb$, $qb$Finish the one closest to done, so at least one person stops waiting$qb$, $qb$Finish the tasks in the order that other people are waiting on them$qb$, $qb$Work out how much is left on each before deciding what to do next$qb$, $qb$Spread your time across all five so none of them falls further behind$qb$, $qb$Continue as you are, since all five are moving forward together$qb$, 5, 3, 2, 1, 0, true),
  ($qb$HEAIL-ECF-MCQ-020$qb$, $qb$A7-01$qb$, $qb$MCQ$qb$, $qb$A colleague asks you to take on a new task while three of yours are nearly complete. What should you do?$qb$, $qb$Finish the three, tell them when you can start, and hold to that$qb$, $qb$Finish the three first and then take on the new task$qb$, $qb$Ask when the new task is needed by before agreeing to take it$qb$, $qb$Take it on now and fit it in alongside the three you are finishing$qb$, $qb$Take it on and return to the three once the new task is under way$qb$, 5, 3, 2, 1, 0, true),
