  ($qb$HEAIL-ECF-MCQ-022$qb$, $qb$A7-01$qb$, $qb$MCQ$qb$, $qb$Your team marks tasks as complete, but work often comes back for corrections. What is the best fix?$qb$, $qb$Agree what 'complete' must include, and check against it before marking$qb$, $qb$Agree a definition of complete that the whole team works to$qb$, $qb$Add a checking step before tasks are marked as complete$qb$, $qb$Ask the team to be more careful before marking work complete$qb$, $qb$Accept the returns, since some rework is normal in any process$qb$, 5, 3, 2, 1, 0, true),
  ($qb$HEAIL-ECF-MCQ-023$qb$, $qb$A7-01$qb$, $qb$MCQ$qb$, $qb$A task you own has been stuck for two weeks waiting on another team. What is the best action?$qb$, $qb$Find out what is blocking them and what would unblock it, then agree a date$qb$, $qb$Contact them to find out what is holding the task up on their side$qb$, $qb$Chase them again and ask when they expect to complete their part$qb$, $qb$Escalate it to your manager, since two weeks is too long to wait$qb$, $qb$Keep waiting, since chasing them further may damage the relationship$qb$, 5, 3, 2, 1, 0, true),
  ($qb$HEAIL-ECF-MCQ-024$qb$, $qb$A7-01$qb$, $qb$MCQ$qb$, $qb$You are three days from a deadline and the work is about half done. What should you do first?$qb$, $qb$Tell whoever is waiting now, so they can decide how to handle it$qb$, $qb$Work out what can realistically be finished in three days$qb$, $qb$Ask your manager whether the deadline can be moved$qb$, $qb$Work longer hours over the three days to close the gap$qb$, $qb$Keep going and report the position once the deadline arrives$qb$, 5, 3, 2, 1, 0, true),
