  ($qb$HEAIL-ROI-FIB-006$qb$, $qb$A7-04$qb$, $qb$FIB$qb$, $qb$Making something work today buys time to arrange the proper fix ______.$qb$, $qb$later$qb$, $qb$cheaply$qb$, $qb$quietly$qb$, $qb$formally$qb$, $qb$manually$qb$, 5, 0, 0, 0, 0, true),
  ($qb$HEAIL-ROI-FIB-007$qb$, $qb$A7-04$qb$, $qb$FIB$qb$, $qb$A quick fix put in to keep things running becomes a problem when nobody writes down that it is ______.$qb$, $qb$temporary$qb$, $qb$urgent$qb$, $qb$unusual$qb$, $qb$cheap$qb$, $qb$shared$qb$, 5, 0, 0, 0, 0, true),
  ($qb$HEAIL-ROI-FIB-009$qb$, $qb$A7-04$qb$, $qb$FIB$qb$, $qb$When money is short, the first place to look is what is already ______.$qb$, $qb$owned$qb$, $qb$ordered$qb$, $qb$budgeted$qb$, $qb$promised$qb$, $qb$counted$qb$, 5, 0, 0, 0, 0, true),
  ($qb$HEAIL-ROI-FIB-012$qb$, $qb$A7-04$qb$, $qb$FIB$qb$, $qb$A limit on one resource often turns out to be a limit on how it is ______.$qb$, $qb$used$qb$, $qb$tested$qb$, $qb$labelled$qb$, $qb$reported$qb$, $qb$scheduled$qb$, 5, 0, 0, 0, 0, true),
  ($qb$HEAIL-ROI-FIB-013$qb$, $qb$A7-04$qb$, $qb$FIB$qb$, $qb$Finding out how long the shortage will last decides whether to work around it or ______ it.$qb$, $qb$wait$qb$, $qb$report$qb$, $qb$price$qb$, $qb$document$qb$, $qb$file$qb$, 5, 0, 0, 0, 0, true),
  ($qb$HEAIL-ROI-FIB-014$qb$, $qb$A7-04$qb$, $qb$FIB$qb$, $qb$The cheapest solution is sometimes the one that removes the need for the job ______.$qb$, $qb$entirely$qb$, $qb$today$qb$, $qb$twice$qb$, $qb$publicly$qb$, $qb$manually$qb$, 5, 0, 0, 0, 0, true),
  ($qb$HEAIL-ROI-FIB-015$qb$, $qb$A7-04$qb$, $qb$FIB$qb$, $qb$Testing an improvised method on a small part first limits what a failure can ______.$qb$, $qb$damage$qb$, $qb$prove$qb$, $qb$test$qb$, $qb$fix$qb$, $qb$stop$qb$, 5, 0, 0, 0, 0, true),
  ($qb$HEAIL-ROI-FIB-016$qb$, $qb$A7-04$qb$, $qb$FIB$qb$, $qb$A supplier who cannot meet the whole order may still be able to send ______.$qb$, $qb$part$qb$, $qb$later$qb$, $qb$cheaper$qb$, $qb$notice$qb$, $qb$advice$qb$, 5, 0, 0, 0, 0, true),
  ($qb$HEAIL-ROI-FIB-017$qb$, $qb$A7-04$qb$, $qb$FIB$qb$, $qb$Knowing what a job genuinely requires separates a real limit from an assumed ______.$qb$, $qb$one$qb$, $qb$label$qb$, $qb$job$qb$, $qb$requirement$qb$, $qb$skill$qb$, 5, 0, 0, 0, 0, true),
  ($qb$HEAIL-ROI-FIB-018$qb$, $qb$A7-04$qb$, $qb$FIB$qb$, $qb$When the usual supplier cannot deliver in time, asking what the item is needed ______ can open up other options.$qb$, $qb$for$qb$, $qb$from$qb$, $qb$twice$qb$, $qb$about$qb$, $qb$with$qb$, 5, 0, 0, 0, 0, true),
  ($qb$HEAIL-ROI-MCQ-019$qb$, $qb$A7-04$qb$, $qb$MCQ$qb$, $qb$You run a small café. The coffee machine has broken and the repair engineer cannot come until tomorrow morning. You open in an hour. What is the most useful first step?$qb$, $qb$Find out what you can still serve, and put a sign up saying what is off today$qb$, $qb$Work out which drinks on the menu do not need the machine at all$qb$, $qb$Ring other repair firms to see whether anyone can come out today$qb$, $qb$Ring the engineer back and ask them to treat it as an emergency$qb$, $qb$Close for the day, since a café without coffee cannot really trade$qb$, 5, 3, 2, 1, 0, true),
  ($qb$HEAIL-ROI-MCQ-020$qb$, $qb$A7-04$qb$, $qb$MCQ$qb$, $qb$A form requires a manager's signature. Your manager is away for a week and the work cannot wait. What should you do?$qb$, $qb$Find out who can sign in their absence, since most rules name a deputy$qb$, $qb$Ask whether anyone else has authority to sign while your manager is away$qb$, $qb$Email your manager and ask them to approve it while they are away$qb$, $qb$Sign it yourself and explain to your manager when they return$qb$, $qb$Wait the week, since the form clearly requires a manager's signature$qb$, 5, 3, 2, 1, 0, true),
  ($qb$HEAIL-ROI-MCQ-021$qb$, $qb$A7-04$qb$, $qb$MCQ$qb$, $qb$You need to move twelve boxes across a site. The trolley is being used by another team for the next two hours. The boxes must move within the hour. What is the best approach?$qb$, $qb$Ask the other team when they next pause, and move what you can by hand meanwhile$qb$, $qb$Start carrying the boxes by hand, since the deadline is inside the hour$qb$, $qb$Ask the other team whether you could borrow the trolley for ten minutes$qb$, $qb$Wait for the trolley, since carrying twelve boxes by hand will take too long$qb$, $qb$Tell the person waiting that the boxes will be late because of the trolley$qb$, 5, 3, 2, 1, 0, true),
  ($qb$HEAIL-ROI-MCQ-022$qb$, $qb$A7-04$qb$, $qb$MCQ$qb$, $qb$Your team needs software that costs money you do not have this quarter. What is the most useful thing to establish first?$qb$, $qb$What the software would actually do, since part of it may already be possible$qb$, $qb$Whether a free or cheaper version would cover what the team needs$qb$, $qb$Whether the cost could be met from another part of the budget$qb$, $qb$How much of the work could be done by hand until next quarter$qb$, $qb$When the budget resets, so the purchase can be made then$qb$, 5, 3, 2, 1, 0, true),
  ($qb$HEAIL-ROI-MCQ-023$qb$, $qb$A7-04$qb$, $qb$MCQ$qb$, $qb$A customer wants a product in a colour you do not stock and cannot order for three weeks. What is the best response?$qb$, $qb$Ask what the colour is for, since another option may serve the same purpose$qb$, $qb$Tell them the wait is three weeks and ask whether that works for them$qb$, $qb$Offer them the colours you do have in stock right now$qb$, $qb$Order it and tell them it will be three weeks before it arrives$qb$, $qb$Tell them you cannot supply that colour and suggest another shop$qb$, 5, 3, 2, 1, 0, true),
  ($qb$HEAIL-ROI-MCQ-024$qb$, $qb$A7-04$qb$, $qb$MCQ$qb$, $qb$A machine on your line has failed. A spare part exists but is two days away. The line makes four products, and only one of them uses that machine. What should you do?$qb$, $qb$Switch the line to the three products that do not need that machine$qb$, $qb$Work out which products can still be made while the part is coming$qb$, $qb$Ask the supplier whether the part can be delivered any faster$qb$, $qb$Stop the line until the part arrives in two days' time$qb$, $qb$Run the machine carefully and hope it lasts until the part arrives$qb$, 5, 3, 2, 1, 0, true),
  ($qb$HEAIL-ROI-MCQ-025$qb$, $qb$A7-04$qb$, $qb$MCQ$qb$, $qb$You need data that sits in a system you do not have access to. Getting access takes two weeks. You need the data on Friday. What is the best step?$qb$, $qb$Ask someone with access to pull the specific figures you need this week$qb$, $qb$Request access now and ask a colleague to help you in the meantime$qb$, $qb$Ask whether the data exists anywhere else you can already reach$qb$, $qb$Request access and tell the person waiting that Friday is not possible$qb$, $qb$Wait for access, since going through someone else may not be permitted$qb$, 5, 3, 2, 1, 0, true),
  ($qb$HEAIL-ROI-MCQ-026$qb$, $qb$A7-04$qb$, $qb$MCQ$qb$, $qb$A training room you booked is double-booked and the other group arrived first. Twelve people are arriving in fifteen minutes. What is the best action?$qb$, $qb$Find any space that holds twelve, and message the group where to go$qb$, $qb$Look for another room that is free and could take the group$qb$, $qb$Ask the other group whether they would be willing to move$qb$, $qb$Ask reception to sort out the booking clash for you quickly$qb$, $qb$Cancel the session and rearrange it for another day$qb$, 5, 3, 2, 1, 0, true),
  ($qb$HEAIL-ROI-MCQ-027$qb$, $qb$A7-04$qb$, $qb$MCQ$qb$, $qb$Your delivery van is off the road for repairs for two days. You have eight local deliveries due. What should you look at first?$qb$, $qb$Which deliveries genuinely need the van, since some may be walkable or postable$qb$, $qb$Whether a van can be hired for the two days the vehicle is off the road$qb$, $qb$Whether any of the eight deliveries could wait until the van returns$qb$, $qb$How much a courier would cost for all eight deliveries$qb$, $qb$Telling all eight customers that their delivery will be two days late$qb$, 5, 3, 2, 1, 0, true),
  ($qb$HEAIL-ROI-MCQ-028$qb$, $qb$A7-04$qb$, $qb$MCQ$qb$, $qb$You are asked to produce a report by Thursday. The usual template is on a shared drive that is down until Friday. What is the best response?$qb$, $qb$Ask a colleague for a saved copy first, and rebuild only if nobody has one$qb$, $qb$Rebuild a simple version of the template so the report can be written$qb$, $qb$Ask a colleague whether they have a copy of the template saved locally$qb$, $qb$Write the report without a template and format it when the drive returns$qb$, $qb$Tell the requester the report will be late because the drive is down$qb$, 5, 3, 2, 1, 0, true),
  ($qb$HEAIL-ROI-MCQ-029$qb$, $qb$A7-04$qb$, $qb$MCQ$qb$, $qb$Your budget for a team event has been halved. The event was to include a venue, food and a speaker. What is the best approach?$qb$, $qb$Ask what the event is meant to achieve, then spend the money on that part$qb$, $qb$Work out which of the three elements matters most and keep that one$qb$, $qb$Reduce the spending on all three so that the event still happens$qb$, $qb$Ask for the original budget to be restored so the event can go ahead$qb$, $qb$Cancel the event, since half the budget will not deliver what was planned$qb$, 5, 3, 2, 1, 0, true),
  ($qb$HEAIL-ROI-MCQ-030$qb$, $qb$A7-04$qb$, $qb$MCQ$qb$, $qb$A supplier can deliver only sixty per cent of your order this week. What should you find out first?$qb$, $qb$Which of your customers need it soonest, so the sixty per cent goes where it counts$qb$, $qb$Whether the remaining forty per cent will arrive next week$qb$, $qb$Whether another supplier could make up the shortfall$qb$, $qb$How much the shortfall will cost you in lost sales$qb$, $qb$Whether the supplier can be held to the full order this week$qb$, 5, 3, 2, 1, 0, true),
  ($qb$HEAIL-ROI-MCQ-031$qb$, $qb$A7-04$qb$, $qb$MCQ$qb$, $qb$Your team of six is down to four for a week because two are ill. The workload is unchanged. What is the best first step?$qb$, $qb$Identify what can safely wait a week, and tell those affected it is waiting$qb$, $qb$Work out what the four people can realistically get through this week$qb$, $qb$Ask another team whether they can lend anyone for the week$qb$, $qb$Ask the four to take on the extra work between them for the week$qb$, $qb$Carry on and see how much the four manage to complete$qb$, 5, 3, 2, 1, 0, true),
  ($qb$HEAIL-ROI-MCQ-032$qb$, $qb$A7-04$qb$, $qb$MCQ$qb$, $qb$You need to print two hundred booklets by tomorrow. Your printer handles fifty a day. What is the best approach?$qb$, $qb$Find out how many are needed tomorrow, since the rest may not be needed at once$qb$, $qb$Print fifty overnight and send the remaining hundred and fifty out to a print shop$qb$, $qb$Send the whole job to an outside print shop that can meet the deadline$qb$, $qb$Run your printer overnight and deliver what is ready in the morning$qb$, $qb$Tell the requester that two hundred by tomorrow is not achievable$qb$, 5, 3, 2, 1, 0, true),
  ($qb$HEAIL-ROI-MCQ-033$qb$, $qb$A7-04$qb$, $qb$MCQ$qb$, $qb$A customer has a problem your company does not normally handle, and no process covers it. What is the best response?$qb$, $qb$Work out what the customer actually needs, then find who could provide it$qb$, $qb$Find out whether anyone in the company has dealt with something similar$qb$, $qb$Ask your manager how they would like this handled this time$qb$, $qb$Tell the customer this falls outside what the company can offer$qb$, $qb$Follow the closest existing process, even if it does not quite fit$qb$, 5, 3, 2, 1, 0, true),
  ($qb$HEAIL-ROI-MCQ-034$qb$, $qb$A7-04$qb$, $qb$MCQ$qb$, $qb$Your team must complete a task that normally needs three people. Only two are available. The task cannot be split. What should you establish first?$qb$, $qb$Why three are normally needed, since one may be there for a reason that has changed$qb$, $qb$Whether two people could complete it if given more time to do so$qb$, $qb$Whether a third person could be borrowed from elsewhere for the task$qb$, $qb$How much longer two people would take than the usual three$qb$, $qb$That the task cannot be done, since three people are clearly required$qb$, 5, 3, 2, 1, 0, true),
  ($qb$HEAIL-ROI-MCQ-035$qb$, $qb$A7-04$qb$, $qb$MCQ$qb$, $qb$Your card payment terminal has stopped working and cannot be repaired until Monday. What matters most in deciding what to do this weekend?$qb$, $qb$How many of your customers pay by card$qb$, $qb$Whether another way of taking card payment can be set up quickly$qb$, $qb$How much trade you would lose by closing until Monday$qb$, $qb$Whether the provider can be persuaded to attend sooner$qb$, $qb$Whether customers will understand that it is not your fault$qb$, 5, 3, 2, 1, 0, true),
  ($qb$HEAIL-ROI-MCQ-036$qb$, $qb$A7-04$qb$, $qb$MCQ$qb$, $qb$A customer asks you for a product you do not stock. What is the most useful thing to find out before answering?$qb$, $qb$What he intends to use it for$qb$, $qb$When he needs it by$qb$, $qb$Whether he has tried other shops$qb$, $qb$Which brand he prefers$qb$, $qb$Whether he is a regular customer$qb$, 5, 3, 2, 1, 0, true),
  ($qb$HEAIL-ROI-MCQ-037$qb$, $qb$A7-04$qb$, $qb$MCQ$qb$, $qb$A regular process you run depends on a paper form that has run out. Reprinting takes four days. The process runs daily. What is the best action?$qb$, $qb$Record the same information another way, and note that the form is outstanding$qb$, $qb$Write the information on plain paper until the forms are reprinted$qb$, $qb$Photocopy an existing blank form to cover the four days$qb$, $qb$Ask whether the process can pause for four days until forms arrive$qb$, $qb$Stop the process until the printed forms are available again$qb$, 5, 3, 2, 1, 0, true),
  ($qb$HEAIL-ROI-SJT-038$qb$, $qb$A7-04$qb$, $qb$SJT$qb$, $qb$You run a small guest house with six rooms. Your only washing machine has broken on a Friday afternoon. The repair firm cannot attend until Monday. You have four rooms changing over on Saturday morning and enough clean linen for two. How do you handle this?$qb$, $qb$Find a laundry or a neighbour's machine today, and set out what is needed by when$qb$, $qb$Take the linen to a launderette on Saturday morning before the changeovers$qb$, $qb$Ring around to find a laundry that could take the washing over the weekend$qb$, $qb$Change over the two rooms you have linen for and delay the other two$qb$, $qb$Tell the two guests without clean linen that their rooms are not ready$qb$, 5, 3, 2, 1, 0, true),
  ($qb$HEAIL-ROI-SJT-039$qb$, $qb$A7-04$qb$, $qb$SJT$qb$, $qb$You are a site foreman. A concrete delivery has arrived two hours early and the ground is not yet prepared. Concrete sets in about ninety minutes. Your crew of five are on another task that can be paused. How do you handle it?$qb$, $qb$Move the crew onto ground preparation now, since the concrete cannot wait$qb$, $qb$Ask the driver how long the load can safely stay in the mixer$qb$, $qb$Put all five onto preparing the section you can finish in the time$qb$, $qb$Ask the driver to return in two hours when the ground is ready$qb$, $qb$Send the load back, since the site was not ready for an early delivery$qb$, 5, 3, 2, 1, 0, true),
  ($qb$HEAIL-ROI-SJT-040$qb$, $qb$A7-04$qb$, $qb$SJT$qb$, $qb$You manage a school office. The photocopier has broken and forty exam papers are needed for a class in an hour. There is a working printer that prints ten pages a minute. Each paper is four pages. How do you handle it?$qb$, $qb$Print them, since forty papers at four pages takes about sixteen minutes$qb$, $qb$Start printing straight away and see how far you get in the hour$qb$, $qb$Ask another department whether their photocopier is free to use$qb$, $qb$Ask the teacher whether the class could share papers between pairs$qb$, $qb$Tell the teacher the papers cannot be produced in time today$qb$, 5, 3, 2, 1, 0, true),
  ($qb$HEAIL-ROI-SJT-041$qb$, $qb$A7-04$qb$, $qb$SJT$qb$, $qb$You work in a pharmacy. A regular customer needs a medicine you have run out of. Your supplier delivers tomorrow morning. Another branch four miles away has it in stock, and the customer says they cannot travel. How do you handle it?$qb$, $qb$Ask the other branch to send it over, or arrange to collect it yourself today$qb$, $qb$Ring the other branch and ask whether they can transfer the medicine here$qb$, $qb$Ask the customer whether the medicine can wait until tomorrow morning$qb$, $qb$Tell the customer the other branch has it and give them the address$qb$, $qb$Tell the customer to come back tomorrow when the delivery arrives$qb$, 5, 3, 2, 1, 0, true),
  ($qb$HEAIL-ROI-SJT-042$qb$, $qb$A7-04$qb$, $qb$SJT$qb$, $qb$You manage a small charity. A grant of a fixed amount must be spent by month end or returned. The equipment you planned to buy is out of stock until next month. How do you handle it?$qb$, $qb$Check what the grant terms actually allow, then spend it on something they permit$qb$, $qb$Ask the funder whether the deadline can be extended by a month$qb$, $qb$Look for an alternative supplier who has the equipment in stock$qb$, $qb$Buy a different model that is available, whether or not it suits$qb$, $qb$Return the grant, since the planned purchase cannot be made in time$qb$, 5, 3, 2, 1, 0, true),
  ($qb$HEAIL-ROI-SJT-043$qb$, $qb$A7-04$qb$, $qb$SJT$qb$, $qb$You are a hotel receptionist on a night shift. The booking system has gone down and six guests are due to arrive over the next two hours. You have a printed arrivals list from this morning. How do you handle it?$qb$, $qb$Check the guests in against the printed list and record everything on paper$qb$, $qb$Use the printed list to check in guests and enter it all when the system returns$qb$, $qb$Ring the manager to ask how they would like the arrivals handled$qb$, $qb$Ask guests for their booking confirmation and check them in from that$qb$, $qb$Ask arriving guests to wait until the booking system comes back up$qb$, 5, 3, 2, 1, 0, true),
  ($qb$HEAIL-ROI-SJT-044$qb$, $qb$A7-04$qb$, $qb$SJT$qb$, $qb$You supervise a warehouse team. A customer needs an urgent order today, but the item is on a high shelf and the forklift is out of service until tomorrow. There is a step ladder rated for the height, and the item weighs three kilograms. How do you handle it?$qb$, $qb$Use the ladder as it is rated for, with a second person steadying it$qb$, $qb$Get the item down using the step ladder since it is light enough$qb$, $qb$Ask whether the customer could take delivery tomorrow instead$qb$, $qb$Have two people reach it without the ladder, since it is only light$qb$, $qb$Tell the customer it cannot go out today because the forklift is down$qb$, 5, 3, 2, 1, 0, true),
  ($qb$HEAIL-ROI-SJT-045$qb$, $qb$A7-04$qb$, $qb$SJT$qb$, $qb$You are a community nurse visiting patients by car. Your car will not start and your first visit is in forty minutes, two miles away. There is a bus that takes twenty minutes and a colleague who drives past that area. How do you handle it?$qb$, $qb$Ask the colleague first, and take the bus if they cannot help in time$qb$, $qb$Take the bus, since it is certain to get you there within the time$qb$, $qb$Ring the colleague and ask whether they could give you a lift today$qb$, $qb$Ring the patient to say you will be late because your car has failed$qb$, $qb$Cancel the visit and rearrange it once your car has been repaired$qb$, 5, 3, 2, 1, 0, true),
  ($qb$HEAIL-ROI-SJT-046$qb$, $qb$A7-04$qb$, $qb$SJT$qb$, $qb$You run a bicycle repair shop. A customer needs a repair today but you do not have the exact replacement part. You have a similar part that fits but is a slightly different colour. How do you handle it?$qb$, $qb$Tell the customer what you have and let them choose between today and matching$qb$, $qb$Offer the part you have and explain that the colour will not match$qb$, $qb$Order the correct part and tell the customer it will be a few days$qb$, $qb$Fit the part you have, since colour makes no difference to how it works$qb$, $qb$Tell the customer you cannot do the repair without the correct part$qb$, 5, 3, 2, 1, 0, true),
  ($qb$HEAIL-ROI-SJT-047$qb$, $qb$A7-04$qb$, $qb$SJT$qb$, $qb$You are a caterer. Sixty guests were booked, but ninety have arrived. You have food for sixty and a supermarket is ten minutes away. Serving starts in forty minutes. How do you handle this?$qb$, $qb$Send someone to buy now, and adjust portions and courses to stretch what you have$qb$, $qb$Send someone to the supermarket immediately for whatever will extend the meal$qb$, $qb$Work out how the existing food could be served across ninety people$qb$, $qb$Serve the sixty portions and explain to the rest that numbers were exceeded$qb$, $qb$Tell the host that only sixty can be served, since that is what was booked$qb$, 5, 3, 2, 1, 0, true),
