  ($qb$HEAIL-ROI-SJT-049$qb$, $qb$A7-04$qb$, $qb$SJT$qb$, $qb$You lead a small design team. Your only colour printer has failed and a client presentation is in two hours. The presentation can be shown on a screen instead of on paper. How do you handle it?$qb$, $qb$Present it on screen, and offer to send the printed copies afterwards$qb$, $qb$Show it on screen for the meeting rather than trying to print it$qb$, $qb$Find a print shop that could produce the copies within two hours$qb$, $qb$Print it in black and white so there is something on paper$qb$, $qb$Ask the client to move the presentation to another day$qb$, 5, 3, 2, 1, 0, true),
  ($qb$HEAIL-ROI-SJT-050$qb$, $qb$A7-04$qb$, $qb$SJT$qb$, $qb$You work in a call centre. The system that logs calls has gone down and is expected back tomorrow morning. Calls are still coming in and each one normally needs a record. How do you handle it?$qb$, $qb$Keep the records on paper with the same details, and enter them when it returns$qb$, $qb$Write down the details of each call so they can be entered later$qb$, $qb$Ask the team leader how calls should be recorded while it is down$qb$, $qb$Take the calls and rely on memory to enter them once it is working$qb$, $qb$Stop taking calls until the logging system is back in service$qb$, 5, 3, 2, 1, 0, true),
