  ($qb$HEAIL-AFM-MCQ-020$qb$, $qb$A7-06$qb$, $qb$MCQ$qb$, $qb$What most reliably damages the quality of demanding work?$qb$, $qb$Switching between it and something else$qb$, $qb$Doing it when you are tired$qb$, $qb$Doing it under time pressure$qb$, $qb$Doing it in a noisy place$qb$, $qb$Doing it without a clear plan$qb$, 5, 3, 2, 1, 0, true),
  ($qb$HEAIL-AFM-MCQ-021$qb$, $qb$A7-06$qb$, $qb$MCQ$qb$, $qb$A thought about another task keeps intruding while you work. What is best?$qb$, $qb$Write it down and return to what you are doing$qb$, $qb$Deal with it quickly so it stops intruding$qb$, $qb$Note it mentally and carry on$qb$, $qb$Ignore it until it fades$qb$, $qb$Stop and think it through properly$qb$, 5, 3, 2, 1, 0, true),
  ($qb$HEAIL-AFM-MCQ-022$qb$, $qb$A7-06$qb$, $qb$MCQ$qb$, $qb$You have one demanding task and several small ones. What order is usually best?$qb$, $qb$The demanding one first, while your attention is freshest$qb$, $qb$Clear the small ones so your mind is free$qb$, $qb$Whichever of them is most urgent$qb$, $qb$Alternate so that neither becomes stale$qb$, $qb$The quickest ones, to reduce the list$qb$, 5, 3, 2, 1, 0, true),
