  ($qb$HEAIL-EMB-MCQ-030$qb$, $qb$A7-07$qb$, $qb$MCQ$qb$, $qb$What most helps a team through a period of sustained heavy work?$qb$, $qb$Knowing what happens when it ends$qb$, $qb$Being thanked regularly for the effort$qb$, $qb$Being told it is nearly over$qb$, $qb$Having extra help brought in$qb$, $qb$Being allowed to work flexible hours$qb$, 5, 3, 2, 1, 0, true),
  ($qb$HEAIL-EMB-MCQ-031$qb$, $qb$A7-07$qb$, $qb$MCQ$qb$, $qb$You notice you have stopped caring about work you used to care about. What does this suggest?$qb$, $qb$You have been running without recovery for too long$qb$, $qb$A holiday is what is needed$qb$, $qb$The work itself has become less interesting$qb$, $qb$A change of role would help$qb$, $qb$This is the wrong job for you$qb$, 5, 3, 2, 1, 0, true),
  ($qb$HEAIL-EMB-MCQ-032$qb$, $qb$A7-07$qb$, $qb$MCQ$qb$, $qb$A deadline can only be met by everyone working through the weekend. What is best?$qb$, $qb$Say what next week loses if everyone works this weekend$qb$, $qb$Ask the team whether they are willing$qb$, $qb$Work the weekend and take time back after$qb$, $qb$Ask for the deadline to be moved$qb$, $qb$Work the weekend, since the deadline is fixed$qb$, 5, 3, 2, 1, 0, true),
  ($qb$HEAIL-EMB-MCQ-033$qb$, $qb$A7-07$qb$, $qb$MCQ$qb$, $qb$What tells you most about someone's workload over a month?$qb$, $qb$What they have stopped doing without deciding to$qb$, $qb$How many hours they have worked$qb$, $qb$How much they have completed$qb$, $qb$Whether they have missed deadlines$qb$, $qb$Whether they say they are busy$qb$, 5, 3, 2, 1, 0, true),
  ($qb$HEAIL-EMB-MCQ-034$qb$, $qb$A7-07$qb$, $qb$MCQ$qb$, $qb$You are asked to do something in your own time that should be paid work. What is best?$qb$, $qb$Say what it is and ask how it should be resourced$qb$, $qb$Do it, since it needs doing$qb$, $qb$Decline and explain why$qb$, $qb$Do it once and raise it if it recurs$qb$, $qb$Ask a colleague whether they would do it$qb$, 5, 3, 2, 1, 0, true),
  ($qb$HEAIL-EMB-MCQ-035$qb$, $qb$A7-07$qb$, $qb$MCQ$qb$, $qb$What is the main risk of a manager who visibly never stops working?$qb$, $qb$The team learns that stopping is not acceptable$qb$, $qb$The manager becomes exhausted$qb$, $qb$The manager loses perspective$qb$, $qb$The team feels it cannot keep up$qb$, $qb$The manager takes on too much$qb$, 5, 3, 2, 1, 0, true),
  ($qb$HEAIL-EMB-MCQ-036$qb$, $qb$A7-07$qb$, $qb$MCQ$qb$, $qb$You have three heavy weeks ahead and cannot avoid them. What is most useful now?$qb$, $qb$Decide now what you will drop during those weeks$qb$, $qb$Prepare as much as possible in advance$qb$, $qb$Arrange recovery time for afterwards$qb$, $qb$Tell people you will be less available$qb$, $qb$Get as much rest as you can beforehand$qb$, 5, 3, 2, 1, 0, true),
  ($qb$HEAIL-EMB-SJT-037$qb$, $qb$A7-07$qb$, $qb$SJT$qb$, $qb$You lead a fruit picking crew. The season runs eight weeks and by week three the crew are slowing and making mistakes with grading. Rates are paid on weight. How do you respond?$qb$, $qb$Change the pattern of the day so the crew can hold the eight weeks$qb$, $qb$Introduce a short break every two hours$qb$, $qb$Tell the crew that grading errors are costing them$qb$, $qb$Ask the crew to pace themselves better$qb$, $qb$Push on, since the season is only eight weeks$qb$, 5, 3, 2, 1, 0, true),
  ($qb$HEAIL-EMB-SJT-038$qb$, $qb$A7-07$qb$, $qb$SJT$qb$, $qb$You manage hotel housekeeping. Rooms have been added without extra staff and your team has worked through breaks for a month. How do you respond?$qb$, $qb$Set out what the room count needs, and what is not being done$qb$, $qb$Insist that breaks are taken$qb$, $qb$Ask for extra staff during busy weeks$qb$, $qb$Reorganise the rounds to save time$qb$, $qb$Thank the team and keep going until it eases$qb$, 5, 3, 2, 1, 0, true),
  ($qb$HEAIL-EMB-SJT-039$qb$, $qb$A7-07$qb$, $qb$SJT$qb$, $qb$You run a construction site crew. The programme requires six-day weeks for three months. Two of the crew are visibly worn out in week five. How do you respond?$qb$, $qb$Take the six-day requirement back with what week five is showing$qb$, $qb$Rotate the crew so nobody works every sixth day$qb$, $qb$Speak to the two who are struggling$qb$, $qb$Bring in extra labour for the busy weeks$qb$, $qb$Keep going, since the programme is fixed$qb$, 5, 3, 2, 1, 0, true),
  ($qb$HEAIL-EMB-SJT-040$qb$, $qb$A7-07$qb$, $qb$SJT$qb$, $qb$You run a school kitchen. Numbers have risen and your staff now skip their own break to get service out. This has been going on all term. How do you respond?$qb$, $qb$Show what the higher numbers need and ask for the gap to be filled$qb$, $qb$Rearrange preparation so breaks can be taken$qb$, $qb$Insist the team takes its break whatever happens$qb$, $qb$Serve a simpler menu during busy weeks$qb$, $qb$Continue, since service is going out on time$qb$, 5, 3, 2, 1, 0, true),
  ($qb$HEAIL-EMB-SJT-041$qb$, $qb$A7-07$qb$, $qb$SJT$qb$, $qb$You lead a farm harvest team. Weather has compressed the harvest into ten days and the team are working long hours. Day six is when errors usually start. How do you respond?$qb$, $qb$Plan the ten days so the heaviest work falls before day six$qb$, $qb$Add a rest day in the middle of the ten$qb$, $qb$Warn the team that errors rise around day six$qb$, $qb$Bring in extra hands for the second half$qb$, $qb$Work straight through, since the weather decides$qb$, 5, 3, 2, 1, 0, true),
  ($qb$HEAIL-EMB-SJT-042$qb$, $qb$A7-07$qb$, $qb$SJT$qb$, $qb$You run a shutdown maintenance crew. The shutdown is four days of continuous work and your crew have done three in a row this month. How do you respond?$qb$, $qb$Say plainly that a fourth in a row is not safe to staff$qb$, $qb$Ask for extra crew for the fourth shutdown$qb$, $qb$Rotate who works the fourth shutdown$qb$, $qb$Shorten the shifts within the fourth shutdown$qb$, $qb$Take it on, since the crew have managed three$qb$, 5, 3, 2, 1, 0, true),
  ($qb$HEAIL-EMB-SJT-043$qb$, $qb$A7-07$qb$, $qb$SJT$qb$, $qb$You run a removals company. Summer is your peak and your crews work six days a week for ten weeks. Bookings have grown again this year. How do you respond?$qb$, $qb$Decide now how many jobs the crews can hold, and book to that$qb$, $qb$Take on seasonal staff for the peak$qb$, $qb$Spread bookings further across the week$qb$, $qb$Pay extra for the sixth day$qb$, $qb$Take the bookings and manage the pressure$qb$, 5, 3, 2, 1, 0, true),
  ($qb$HEAIL-EMB-SJT-044$qb$, $qb$A7-07$qb$, $qb$SJT$qb$, $qb$You maintain an ice rink. You work early mornings and late nights with a long gap in between, so your day is split into two. You have done this for two years and are constantly tired. How do you respond?$qb$, $qb$Ask for the day to be arranged as one shift instead of two$qb$, $qb$Use the gap between the two parts to rest properly$qb$, $qb$Ask for the early and late duties to be split between two people$qb$, $qb$Improve your sleep at night$qb$, $qb$Continue, since the rink needs both shifts covered$qb$, 5, 3, 2, 1, 0, true),
  ($qb$HEAIL-EMB-SJT-045$qb$, $qb$A7-07$qb$, $qb$SJT$qb$, $qb$You supervise a brewery bottling shift. Output targets rose in January and the line has run flat out since. Two of your six have been off sick this month. How do you respond?$qb$, $qb$Show whoever set the target what the sickness rate is$qb$, $qb$Rotate the hardest positions on the line$qb$, $qb$Ask for a temporary worker to cover$qb$, $qb$Reduce the line speed slightly$qb$, $qb$Continue, since the target is being met$qb$, 5, 3, 2, 1, 0, true),
  ($qb$HEAIL-EMB-SJT-046$qb$, $qb$A7-07$qb$, $qb$SJT$qb$, $qb$You grow tomatoes under glass. Picking runs seven days a week for five months and you and your partner do all of it. You are into month three. How do you respond?$qb$, $qb$Work out now what has to change to reach month five$qb$, $qb$Take one day off each fortnight between you$qb$, $qb$Bring in help for the remaining months$qb$, $qb$Reduce the area you are picking$qb$, $qb$Carry on, since two more months is manageable$qb$, 5, 3, 2, 1, 0, true),
  ($qb$HEAIL-EMB-SJT-047$qb$, $qb$A7-07$qb$, $qb$SJT$qb$, $qb$You manage a theatre box office. The run is six weeks and your two staff have covered every performance so far. There are three weeks left. How do you respond?$qb$, $qb$Arrange cover now rather than at the point they cannot continue$qb$, $qb$Ask them how they are finding it$qb$, $qb$Shorten the hours the office is staffed$qb$, $qb$Bring in a temporary member of staff$qb$, $qb$Continue, since three weeks remain$qb$, 5, 3, 2, 1, 0, true),
  ($qb$HEAIL-EMB-SJT-048$qb$, $qb$A7-07$qb$, $qb$SJT$qb$, $qb$You run an exhibition build crew. Builds are three days of very long hours followed by two quiet weeks. Your crew say the builds are getting harder. How do you respond?$qb$, $qb$Look at what has changed in the builds, not just at the hours$qb$, $qb$Add crew for the three build days$qb$, $qb$Spread the build over four days where possible$qb$, $qb$Ask the crew what would make the builds easier$qb$, $qb$Accept it, since two quiet weeks follow$qb$, 5, 3, 2, 1, 0, true),
  ($qb$HEAIL-EMB-SJT-049$qb$, $qb$A7-07$qb$, $qb$SJT$qb$, $qb$You run an overnight breakdown recovery service. Callouts are unpredictable and drivers sleep badly between them. The winter has eight weeks to run. How do you respond?$qb$, $qb$Set a limit on consecutive callouts and staff to it$qb$, $qb$Give drivers longer between callouts where possible$qb$, $qb$Ask drivers to rest properly during the day$qb$, $qb$Bring in additional drivers for the winter$qb$, $qb$Continue, since callouts cannot be predicted$qb$, 5, 3, 2, 1, 0, true),
  ($qb$HEAIL-EMB-SJT-050$qb$, $qb$A7-07$qb$, $qb$SJT$qb$, $qb$You manage a seasonal card shop. The last six weeks of the year are frantic and your staff are students with exams. Two have asked for fewer hours. How do you respond?$qb$, $qb$Build the roster around what they can actually sustain$qb$, $qb$Recruit additional staff for the six weeks$qb$, $qb$Grant the two requests and cover the gaps$qb$, $qb$Ask them to manage until the season ends$qb$, $qb$Offer higher pay for the busiest shifts$qb$, 5, 3, 2, 1, 0, true)
